  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Hana, I've verified your account and looked into order Q-7501.\n\nThe courier's records show the order was left at your door at 7:02 PM. They took a photo of a bag at the door of apartment 1204. Because of that photo, I can't refund or credit the order myself.\n\nI've passed your case to a specialist as a delivery dispute. They'll follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'll decide.\n\nWhile you wait, you could check with neighbors or the front desk, and look around the building entrance or nearby doors in case the bag was moved."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "The order number is 7501, not Q-7501, but whatever. I checked my door at 7:10 and there was nothing there. The photo must be of someone else's door, or it's a different bag.\n\nPackages have gone missing in this building before, so I'm not surprised it happened again. But I didn't get this pizza and I want a full refund, not a 24-hour wait."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why you're frustrated, Hana. You're out a meal and you've had to wait. The order is Q-7501 in our system, and that's the one I escalated.\n\nI can't issue a refund on this order. The courier's record shows a handoff with a photo of the bag at the door of apartment 1204. When that proof exists and a customer says the order never arrived, a specialist has to review it. I can't decide it myself, and I can't speed up that review.\n\nI've added what you told me to the case. That includes your check at 7:10, your concern that the photo may show a different door or bag, and the earlier package thefts in your building. The specialist will follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise the outcome, but your account of it is part of the case.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so I'm supposed to just wait a day and hope. You've already pushed it to a specialist, so I'll accept that for now, but I'm not happy about it.\n\nPlease make sure they know I checked my door at 7:10 and found nothing. If they come back and say I'm lying about the photo, I'll be following up hard.\n\nThanks for at least adding my notes to the case."
  }
